    "content": {
      "value": "This page defines the confirmed SFCC product attribute set for the Zimmermann platform, derived from the Magento product export (`sfccexport.csv`) and verified against the Magento staging REST API (`/rest/V1/products/attributes/{code}`). It is a child of the TSD: Product — SFCC Catalogue & Data Integration page.\n\n**Attribute types confirmed via:**`frontend_input` from Magento REST API — `select` → `enum-of-string`, `textarea` → `text`, `boolean` → `boolean`, `text` → `string`.\n\nThe conversion script lives at `scripts/magento-to-sfcc.js` in the [zimmermann-sfcc](https://github.com/ZimmermannAU/zimmermann-sfcc/) repository.\n\n---\n\n1. Attribute Source Authority\n-----------------------------\n\nThe **Source** column across all tables in this page uses the following controlled values. Understanding which system owns each attribute is critical for data import design, job scheduling, and Business Manager governance.\n\n| Source Value | Meaning | Who writes it | When it changes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **AP21** | Data originates in AP21 ERP and is imported into SFCC via MuleSoft. SFCC holds a read copy — AP21 is the system of record. | MuleSoft product import job | On product creation or AP21 product update |\n| **AP21 → SFCC (derived)** | Raw data originates in AP21 but the SFCC value is computed during import (e.g. splitting a field, stripping HTML, mapping a code to a label). AP21 remains the source of truth; MuleSoft/import logic owns the transformation. | MuleSoft product import job (with transform logic) | On product creation or AP21 product update |\n| **SFCC** | Value is set and maintained entirely within SFCC — either hardcoded by product type, configured in Business Manager, or set manually by the merchandising team. AP21 has no visibility of this field. | Merchandiser in Business Manager, or SFCC platform logic | On explicit BM update or SFCC job run |\n| **NewStore** | Value is written into SFCC by the NewStore inventory/availability integration, not by AP21 or the product import. | NewStore → SFCC inventory sync job | On stock movement or availability event |\n\n### Source split summary\n\nThe vast majority of product attributes — product identity, naming, descriptions, variation structure, taxonomy codes, care/fabric/fit content, pricing signals, and flags — originate in **AP21**. The only attributes that are not AP21-sourced are:\n\n* **SFCC-owned:**`searchable-flag`, `tax-class-id` (overrideable in BM), `sizeGuide` (set in BM by merch team), product images (loaded directly into SFCC), `colourFilter`, `materialFilter`\n* **AP21 → SFCC (derived):**`online-flag`, `display-name`, `page-title`, `page-url`, `color`, `refinementColor`, `careInstructions`, `sizeFit`\n* **NewStore-owned:**`available-flag`\n* **Merch content (editorial copy):**`long-description` (`webnote`), `short-description`, `story`, `stylingNotes` (`stylnot`) — these fields arrive via AP21 but their content is authored by the Zimmermann merchandising/editorial team upstream of AP21\n\n---\n\n2. Product Hierarchy & ID Conventions\n-------------------------------------\n\n| SFCC Role | ID Pattern | Magento Equivalent | Example |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Master product | `stylecode` | Derived — does not exist as a Magento row | `4673TS251` |\n| Variation group (colour group) | `stylecode` + `colourcode` | Style + colour SKU — `visibility = Catalog, Search` | `4673TS251GVSCP` |\n| Variant | `stylecode` + `colourcode` + `sizecode` | Style + colour + size SKU — `visibility = Not Visible Individually` | `4673TS251GVSCP0P` |\n\n**Purpose of each level:** - **Master** — holds variation attributes (colour, size), images, descriptions, SEO fields - **Variation group** — source of images, editorial descriptions, variation attributes - **Variant** — individual purchasable SKU; carries price, inventory, GTIN\n\n---\n\n3. SFCC System Attributes (Built-in Catalogue XML Elements)\n-----------------------------------------------------------\n\nThese map to standard SFCC catalogue XML elements — no custom `system-objecttype-extensions.xml` entry required.\n\n| **Attribute Name** | **SFCC Attribute Id** | **SFCC Element** | **Sample Data** | **Data Type** | **Hierarchy Level** | **Is Searchable** | **Is Filterable** | **Source** | **Magento Field** | **Notes** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Product ID (master) | ID | `product-id` | 4673TS251 | String | Master | No | No | **AP21** | `stylecode` | Stylecode **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| Product ID (colour variant) | ID | `product-id` | 4673TS251GVSCP | String | Variant Group | No | No | **AP21** | `configurable sku` | Product code + colour code **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| Product ID (variant) | ID | `product-id` | 4673TS251GVSCP0P | String | Variant | No | No | **AP21** | `simple sku` | Product code + colour code + size code **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| Display Name | name | `display-name` | Illuminate Fitted Blouse-Guava Seascape-0P | String | Master | Yes | No | **AP21 → SFCC (derived)** | `name` | Strip `- ColourName - SizeCodeName`suffix for the simple product name **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| Long Description | longDescription | `long-description` |  | Text | Master | No | No | **AP21** | `webnote` | Full editorial description — authored by merch team, carried via AP21 **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| Short Description | shortDescription | `short-description` |  | Text | Master | No | No | **AP21** | N/A | New field needed for the designs. We do want short description but not available in m2 today. Also needs to be a new field in AP21 (open item) **Requires MuleSoft mapping** |\n| UPC / GTIN | UPC | `upc` | 9360993226759 | String | Variant | No | No | **AP21** | `gtin` | GTIN barcode - not used from content perspective - wholesale team generates these in AP21, we can map them into SFCC upc field **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| Online Flag | onlineFlag | `online-flag` | Enabled | Boolean | Master / Variant Group / Variant | No | No | **SFCC** | `status` | Set to `true` if `status = Enabled`; overrideable in BM for manual suppression - Updated in Magento today - can also be set at the colour / size level |\n| Searchable Flag | searchable | `searchable-flag` |  | Boolean | Master / Variant | No | No | **SFCC** | — | Hardcoded by product type: `true` on master, `false` on variant **Requires MuleSoft business rule** |\n| Tax Class | taxClassID | `tax-class-id` | Taxable Goods | String | Master | No | No | **AP21 → SFCC (derived)** | `Tax Class` | Default mapped from AP21; overrideable in BM (e.g. zero-rate for UK kids) - attribute is called Tax Class - Taxable Goods is sample value **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| Page Title | pageTitle | `page-title` | Illuminate Fitted Blouse-Guava Seascape-0P | String | Master | No | No | **AP21 → SFCC (derived)** | `name` (stripped) | SEO meta title — strip colour suffix. \\* discuss with Mani. Format: Valiant Wool Scarf Coat Black Online | Zimmermann **Requires MuleSoft business rule & remapping** |\n| Page URL | pageURL | `page-url` | illuminate-fitted-blouse-guava-seascape-0p | String | Master | No | No | **AP21 → SFCC (derived)** | `url_key` (stripped) | Strip colour + size suffixes from Magento url\\_key. base product name and if applicable colour, don't include size Format: illuminate-fitted-blouse-guava-seascape SEO - needs to be checked for SEO requirements **Requires MuleSoft business rule & remapping** |\n| Image (large) | image | `image` | /1/\\_/1.4673ts251.gvscp.guava-seascape.jpg | String (path) | Master | No | No | **SFCC** | `image` | Open item on product images. Directly loaded into SFCC? **Requires MuleSoft business rule** |\n| Image (medium) | image | `image` | /1/\\_/1.4673ts251.gvscp.guava-seascape.jpg | String (path) | Master | No | No | **SFCC** | `small_image` | Open item on product images. Directly loaded into SFCC? **Requires MuleSoft business rule** |\n| Image (small / thumbnail) | image | `image` | /1/\\_/1.4673ts251.gvscp.guava-seascape.jpg | String (path) | Master | No | No | **SFCC** | `thumbnail` | Open item on product images. Directly loaded into SFCC? **Requires MuleSoft business rule** |\n| Image (hi-res / model) | image | `image` | /2/\\_/2.4673ts251.gvscp.guava-seascape.jpg | String (path) | Master | No | No | **SFCC** | `model_image` | Open item on product images. Directly loaded into SFCC? **Requires MuleSoft business rule** |\n| Image (swatch / styling) | image | `image` | /3/\\_/3.4673ts251.gvscp.guava-seascape.jpg | String (path) | Master | No | No | **SFCC** | `product_styling_image` | Open item on product images. Directly loaded into SFCC? **Requires MuleSoft business rule** |\n| Online from | onlineFrom | `online from` |  | Date | Master / Variant Group / Variant | No | No | **SFCC** | N/A | Logic of this field in SFCC: Online flag is leading - if online flag is checked, then this field becomes relevant in the logic to enable a product on the site. If this field is blank, online flag will put the product online regardless. If this field is filled with a future date, product will only be online from that date onwards. **Requires MuleSoft business rule & remapping** |\n| Online to | onlineTo | `online to` |  | Date | Master / Variant Group / Variant | No | No | **SFCC** | N/A | Similar to above explanation but this defines an end date from which the product will not be online any longer. **Requires MuleSoft business rule & remapping** |\n\n\\*need separate deepdive on product images\n\n---\n\n4. Custom Attributes — Already Exist in SFCC\n--------------------------------------------\n\nThese attributes already exist in `system-objecttype-extensions.xml` and do not require new definitions.\n\n| **Attribute ID** | **Description** | **Sample Data** | **SFCC Type** | **Hierarchy Level** | **Is Searchable** | **Is Filterable** | **Source** | **Magento Field** | **Attribute Group** | **Notes** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `color` | Colour code — machine-readable | `GVSCP` | String | Variation Group | Yes | Yes | **AP21 → SFCC (derived)** | `colourcode` | — | Part before `.` in colorcode field - important for looking up product against the buysheet - used for markdown price process **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| `refinementColor` | Colour display name — human-readable | `Guava Seascape` | String | Variation Group | Yes | Yes | **AP21 → SFCC (derived)** | `colourcode` or `colour` | Storefront Attributes | Part after `.`, `_` → space **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| `size` | Size label | `XS` | String | Variant | Yes | Yes | **AP21** | `size` | — | Direct |\n| `styleNumber` | Style code — master product identifier | `4673TS251` | String | Master | No | No | **AP21** | `stylecode` | Storefront Attributes | Direct **Requires MuleSoft remapping** @Victor T. Crisostomo can we change this custom attribute in SFCC to match AP21's stylecode? |\n\n---\n\n5. Custom Attributes — New (Added to `system-objecttype-extensions.xml`)\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nThese are net-new attributes confirmed from the Magento export. All require a new definition in `system-objecttype-extensions.xml`.\n\n| **Attribute ID** | **Description** | **Sample Data** | **SFCC Type** | **Hierarchy Level** | **Is Searchable** | **Is Filterable** | **Source** | **Magento Field** | **Magento Input** | **Attribute Group** | **Notes** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `styleId` | Internal style identifier | `123456` | String | Master and Variantion Group | No | No | **AP21** | `styleid` | text | Zimmermann Product Data | AP21 internal ID — carried through Magento - defaulted populated value - different from stylecode - not used by content team **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| `colourId` | Internal colour identifier | `en` | String | Variation Group | No | No | **AP21** | `colourid` | text | Zimmermann Product Data | AP21 internal ID — carried through Magento - not used by content team **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| `sizeGuide` | Size guide indicator key — identifies which size guide applies to this product | `Kids` | **Enum-of-string. Values:**   * Clothing: OP-4 * Kids * Shoes * Denim * Mens * Onesize * Jewellery * Belts * Gloves * Hats | Master / Variation group | No | No | **SFCC** | `size_guide` | — | Storefront Attributes | Attribute value is a lookup key only. Actual size guide content is authored and stored in **Contentful**. The PWA resolves the Contentful entry using this key at runtime. **Requires MuleSoft business rule & remapping** |\n| `newFromDate` | Start date from which a product is considered new | `2025-03-01` | Date | Master | No | No | **AP21** | `news_from_date` | text | — | Imported from AP21. can be used by SFCC category rules — see open item #7 **Requires MuleSoft business rule & remapping** |\n| `newToDate` | End date after which a product is no longer considered new | `2025-06-30` | Date | Master | No | No | **AP21** | `news_to_date` | text | — | Imported from AP21. Used by SFCC category rules — see open item #7 **Requires MuleSoft business rule & remapping** |\n| `season` | Season code | `SS25` | **Enum-of-string** | Master | No | Yes | **AP21** | `season` | select (114 options) | Zimmermann Product Data | Full option list in `system-objecttype-extensions.xml` Not categories per se - used in magento today to populate disclaimer text on product-badge. It doesn't have to be a dropdown with 114 options - only need the latest seasons - want to be able to filter products on season - also products can be release in one season, but merchandized across seasons. probably around 15-16 different seasons enabled - once all products have been sold/disabled then the season can be disabled. Requires workshop with Dani/Courtney |\n| `label` | Merchandising product line | `Ready to Wear` | **Enum-of-string** | Master | No | Yes | **AP21** | `label` | select (3 options) | Zimmermann Product Data | Options: `Projects`, `Ready to Wear`, `Swim` **To be reviewed with business.** can be kept as categories - coming from AP21 settings - can be used to assign categories - not sure about other use - review by IT? Projects - can be used for collaborations with other brands - Ready to Wear & Swim are the more important ones. **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| `fabricComposition` | Fabric / material composition | `100% Silk` | String | Master | No | No | **AP21** | `content` | select (1480 options) | Storefront Attributes | Kept as string — too many options to enumerate. business - backend field, impacts tax class, team uses this to manually map it to the fabric filters - renaming to fabricComposition is okay **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| `materialFilter` | Filterable material group — maps raw fabric composition to a standard filter value (e.g. Silk, Linen, Cotton) | `Silk` | **Enum-of-string (multi-select)** Values**:** Linen, Silk, Cotton, Wool, Cashmere, Leather, Straw Raffia, Brass, Metal, Terry, Velvet, Denim, Crochet, Patent, Suede, Espadrille, Other, Shiny Lycra, Matte Lycra, Jacquard Lycra, Metallic Lycra, Cotton Crochet, Jersey, Lace | Master / Variant Group | No | Yes | **SFCC** | — |  | Storefront Attributes | Values maintained by Zimmermann merch team. Supports multi-select (e.g. a silk-linen blend maps to both Silk and Linen). Mapping mechanism TBC |\n| `colourFilter` | Filterable colour group — maps raw colour display name to a standard filter value (e.g. Green, Pink, Floral) | `Green` | Enum-of-string (multi-select) Values: Green, White, Black, Floral, Animal Print, Stripe, Dot, Blue, Cream, Gold, Brown, Paisley, Grey, Multi, Pink, Red, Purple | Master / Variant Group | No | Yes | **SFCC** | — |  | Storefront Attributes | Values maintained by Zimmermann merch team. Mapping mechanism TBC (pending confirmation of Magento approach). |\n| `careInstructions` | Garment care instructions | `Dry clean only` | Text | Master | No | No | **AP21** | `care` | textarea | Storefront Attributes | HTML stripped on import - centric 8 into AP21 **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| `countryOfOrigin` | Country of manufacture | `China` | **Enum-of-string** | Master | No | No | **AP21** | `origin` | select (33 countries) | Zimmermann Product Data | Full country list in `system-objecttype-extensions.xml` **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| `sizeFit` | Size and fit guidance |  | Text | Master | No | No | **AP21** | `sizefit` | textarea | Storefront Attributes | HTML stripped on import; authored by merch team, carried via AP21 - content team does webnote upload into AP21 **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| `modelFit` | Model height and sizing text displayed directly on PDP | Model is 5'10\" Tall/177 cm and is wearing a US Size 6, runs true to size. | String | Master | No | No | **AP21** | — | — | New attribute introduced in SFCC-26. Authored by merch team, sourced via AP21. | **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| `nonReturnable` | The item is not returnable | `true` | Boolean | Master | No | Yes | **SFCC** | `final_sale` | boolean | Zimmermann Product Data | `1` → `true`, relates to non-returnable - team manually updates on product \\* Courtney agreed to rename the attribute, it is not final sale - it's non-returnable |\n| `ap21Category` | Internal AP21 ERP category code | `Tops` | String | Master | No | No | **AP21** | `categoryap21` | text | Zimmermann Product Data | Hidden, not searchable — ERP reference only, not storefront nav - top level category (e.g. Tops) **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| `hsCode` | Per-country HS tariff code map | `{AU: 6204.43}` | Text | Master | No | No | **AP21** | `hscodes` | text | Zimmermann Product Data | Used for duty calculation — structured key-value map **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| `environmentalNotes` | Sustainability / environmental notes | `Sustainably sourced` | Text | Master | No | No | **AP21** | `enviro_notes` | text | Storefront Attributes | Currently manual upload into AP21, this is front-end facing, EU/FR site relevant **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| `story` |  | Illuminate | Text | Master | No | No | **AP21** | `story` | text | — | Story / collection name — authored by merch team, carried via AP21 - Story needs to be its own field - this is used for the way we filter the product. It's called stories in magento |\n| `outOfStockStatus` | Unavailable (default), Back in Soon, Coming Soon | Unavailable | **Enum-of-string** | Master / Variant Group | No | No | **SFCC** | `availability` |  | PDP Stock Status | This is used for Back in Soon, Coming Soon - manually set in Magento - different from just inventory. Business does not update in stock/out of stock manually - team manually sets back in soon/coming soon, only 5-10% of the collection goes into reproduction - To avoid going again to \"back in soon\" if product goes out of stock finally, we can introduce a time frame defined for the out-of-stock status |\n| `outOfStockStatusStartDate` | Activation date for a particular out of stock value like Back in Soon, Coming Soon |  | Date/time | Master / Variant Group |  |  | **SFCC** |  |  | PDP Stock Status | New field to capture the activation date for a Coming Soon / Back in Soon status |\n| `outOfStockStatusEndDate` | After this date is reached, reset back to Unavailable |  | Date/time | Master / Variant Group |  |  | **SFCC** |  |  | PDP Stock Status | New field to capture the deactivation date for a Coming Soon / Back in Soon status |\n| `productLine` | Information from AP21 on the Product line | Swim Lycra | String | Master |  |  | AP21 | `prodline` |  | — | This information can be used by the content team to correctly map a product to a category - but this is not a category in itself. This drives the swatch-image set on PDP (apparel vs. Accessories) **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| `productSub` | Further information from AP21 on the Product line | Bikini Triangle | String | Master |  |  | AP21 | `prodsub` |  | — | This information can be used by the content team to correctly map a product to a category - but this is not a category in itself **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| `measurementTable` | This is the content that needs to be on the Size & Fit tab - rendered in a Measurements table | Size, 0P, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4 Waist=65,68,73,78,83, 88 Hip=107,112,117,122,128, 132 Length=100,111,112,113,113, 114 Item measurements have been rounded to the nearest cm |  | Master |  |  | AP21 | `meastab` |  | — | Content team gets measurements table and uploads this into AP21 via webnotes. They have to do conversions between CM and inches - not ideal **Requires MuleSoft remapping** |\n| `sleeve` | This field represents the type of sleeve on a product | Long Sleeve | Enum (Long Sleeve, Short Sleeve, Sleeveless) | Master, Variation Group | No | Yes | SFCC | `sleeve` | select (3 options) |  | This is part of the content enrichment process - and this is a filterable attribute. |\n| `buy` | This is a free text field used to indicate regional launch phases | AU1\\_NH1 | Text | Master, Variation Group | No | Yes | SFCC | `buy` | text |  | Content team uses the buy field in M2 to populate the launch date on those products - that's a bulk update as well - prior to season launch. BUY field (e.g. AU1\\_NH1) - that means it's launching in AU and Northern hemisphere for story 1. They then filter on the buy field and populate the actual storefront launch date in the campaign field (free text, not meant to be used for that). |\n| `relatedColours` | This is a free text field in which products that do not have the same style code can still be linked as related colours. | 8425WRMATLEM,8425WRMATBLH | Text | Master | No | No | SFCC | `related_colours` | 8425WRMATLEM,8425WRMATBLH |  | Manually set by the content team. Impacts colour swatches on PDP |\n\n---\n\n6. Prices (Pricebook — Not Product Attributes)\n----------------------------------------------\n\nPrices are **not** stored as product attributes in SFCC. They are pricebook entries written on **variant** products via MuleSoft from AP21.\n\n**Source: AP21** for all price values. MuleSoft maps AP21 price data → SFCC site → pricebook.\n\n| Store ID (Magento) | SFCC Site | Currency | List Pricebook ID | Sale Pricebook ID |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 0 | ZimmermannAU | AUD | `aud-m-list-prices` | `aud-m-sale-prices` |\n| TBC | ZimmermannUS | USD | `usd-m-list-prices` | `usd-m-sale-prices` |\n| TBC | ZimmermannUK | GBP | `gbp-m-list-prices` | `gbp-m-sale-prices` |\n| TBC | ZimmermannEU | EUR | `eur-m-list-prices` | `eur-m-sale-prices` |\n| TBC | ZimmermannHK | HKD | `hkd-m-list-prices` | `hkd-m-sale-prices` |\n| TBC | ZimmermannME | EUR | `me-eur-m-list-prices` | `me-eur-m-sale-prices` |\n\n* **Regular price** (`price`) → list pricebook on variant — source: **AP21**\n* **Special price** (`special_price`) → sale pricebook when non-null — source: **AP21**\n\n---\n\n7. Attributes NOT in Scope — Managed Elsewhere in SFCC\n------------------------------------------------------\n\nThe following data points are commonly discussed as product attributes but are explicitly **not** stored as product custom attributes. They are managed through separate SFCC mechanisms.\n\n| **Data Point** | **SFCC Mechanism** | **Source** | **Notes** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Price | Pricebook (list + sale) | AP21 | See Section 6 |\n| Stock quantity | Inventory list (NewStore sync) | NewStore | Not a product attribute — updated by NewStore → SFCC inventory job |\n| Stock status with buffer | SFCC inventory availability configuration + job | SFCC | Buffer threshold configured in BM; available qty updated via NewStore import job. Buffer is set in Magento config - varies between regions/season/colour/category/product line of products - set at all level of the categories/products / and should be storefront specific (check artefacts folder) - mulesoft fetch this info from BM and apply to inventory import |\n| \"Sale\" product flag (`isSale`) | Under discussion — see open item #6 | TBC | May be replaced by automated SFCC category rules or promotion qualification rather than a boolean attribute, see open item #6 |\n| Returnable / non-returnable (Enable RMA) | Under discussion — see open item #9 | TBC | Magento `Enable RMA` flag controls whether a return can be initiated on a product. SFCC equivalent mechanism and source system to be confirmed. Open item #9 |\n| Boutique / store stock | MuleSoft `product-availibility-prc-api` | MuleSoft / NewStore | Real-time PDP call — not stored as an attribute - in the inventory lists in SFCC and on the website - realtime call |\n\n---\n\n8. Ignored Magento Fields\n-------------------------\n\nThe following Magento fields are explicitly excluded from the SFCC attribute set. Documented to prevent re-evaluation during future imports.\n\n| **Field** | **Sample Data** | **Reason for Exclusion** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `row_id` | 1726946 | Internal Magento IDs — no SFCC equivalent |\n| `entity_id` | 1724237 | Internal Magento IDs — no SFCC equivalent |\n| `created_in` | 1 | Internal Magento IDs — no SFCC equivalent |\n| `updated_in` | 2147483647 | Internal Magento IDs — no SFCC equivalent |\n| `has_options` | 0 | Not applicable to SFCC simple products |\n| `required_options` | 0 | Not applicable to SFCC simple products |\n| Store rows (non-zero `store_id`) | 0 | Handled per-site via pricebook store mapping |\n| `tier_price` |  | Not used — `special_price` used instead |\n| `gallery`, `old_id`, `minimal_price` |  | Legacy / unused Magento fields |\n| `custom_design*`, `page_layout`, `options_container` |  | Magento presentation config — no SFCC equivalent |\n| `producttabone/two/three/four/five` |  | Tab labels — not content |\n| `vidnote` |  | Handled via separate SFCC content assets |\n| `related_colours`, `colour_swatch_images` |  | Handled via variation attributes |\n| `despwh` |  | Warehouse location — belongs in inventory feed, not product |\n| `lengow_product`, `available_for_toshi` |  | Third-party integrations — separate scope |\n| `campaign`, `coming_soon_flag`, `backin_soon_flag` |  | Handled via SFCC promotions / content slots |\n| `seen_in_block`, `stock_notification_link` |  | Marketing fields — no SFCC equivalent |\n| `visibility` |  | Magento-specific — replaced by `online-flag` and `searchable-flag` in SFCC |\n| `Attribute Set` |  | Magento catalogue organisation — no direct SFCC equivalent |\n| `stylnot` | `Wear with...` | The new designs do not have copy included for this. Does not need to be mapped to SFCC |\n| `Weight` |  | Not used for calculating shipping costs or any other purpose for the content team - can ignore |\n\n---\n\n9. Open Items\n-------------\n\n| **#** | **Item** | **Owner** | **Status** | **Comments** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Confirm Magento `store_id` → SFCC site mapping for stores 6, 9, 12, 18, 19, 22, 25, 28, 35, 38, 40, 43 — required to do data migration | @Tim Lavelle | Open |  |\n| 2 | Confirm `Weight` field — is it required for shipping calculation in SFCC, and does AP21 supply it? | Zimmermann Merch | Closed | 04-08-2026: We don't use this to calculate shipping costs and also the content team does not change this attribute. We don't need it. |\n| 3 | Define controlled value sets (enumeration lists) for `countryOfOrigin` (33 values) — required before `system-objecttype-extensions.xml` is finalised | Integration Lead / Merch | Open |  |\n| 4 | Product imagery source | Zimmermann Digital | Open | Images loaded directly into SFCC static content library? External DAM in the pipeline? |\n| 5 | Stock Status with Buffer | NewStore / SFCC Lead | Closed | Buffer is an SFCC-configured value; available quantity updated via NewStore → SFCC import job |\n| 6 | `isSale` — confirm if attribute can be removed | Zimmermann Merch / Business | Open | Confirm whether `isSale` was a manually curated flag in Magento or derived 